    "blurb": "The show builds to a scorching Turn On Your Lovelight that showcases wild Pigpen energy and a feral Jerry Garcia solo. Recording quality is excellent, offering a clear, well‑balanced capture of the entire concert. Overall performance is high‑energy despite a few early sloppy moments.",
    "review": "April 11, 1970 at the Fillmore West finds the Dead in top form, delivering an electrifying second half that culminates in a blistering Turn On Your Lovelight. Jerry’s guitar roars in a “delightfully feral minor mode,” highlighted by a feedback‑laden solo around the 18‑minute mark, while Pigpen drives the band with his trademark harmonica wails and stage antics that even veer into Zeppelin‑style jam territory. The set flows from a solid first half of folk‑rock numbers into a high‑energy climax, ending on a powerful note despite a slightly sloppy Not Fade Away earlier in the sequence. All three soundboard sources are praised for crystal‑clear mix and faithful dynamics, making this one of the most vivid snapshots of the early ’70 Dead.",
